 inal-style="" fr-original-class="fr-draggable" style="position: relative\;
  max-width: 100%\; cursor: pointer\; padding: 0px 1px\;" /></a></p><p>The 
 <a fr-original-style="" href="https://www.sbchamberfoundation.org/" style=
 "user-select: auto\;"><strong fr-original-style="" style="font-weight: 700
 \;">South Baldwin Chamber Foundation</strong></a> is proud to partner with
  GlenLakes Golf Club to host the <a fr-original-style="" href="https://www
 .sbchamberfoundation.org/golf-fore-education" style="user-select: auto\;">
 <strong fr-original-style="" style="font-weight: 700\;">6th Annual Golf FO
 RE! Education Tournament</strong></a> on November 12\, 2026\, presented by
  <a fr-original-style="" href="https://www.baldwinemc.com/" style="user-se
 lect: auto\;"><strong fr-original-style="" style="font-weight: 700\;">Bald
 win EMC</strong></a>!</p><p>The day will begin with a grab-and-go breakfas
 t at The Pub at GlenLakes\, followed by an 8 AM shotgun start.</p><p>This 
 year&rsquo\;s tournament will be played as a <strong fr-original-style="" 
 style="font-weight: 700\;">four-man scramble</strong>. Players will enjoy 
 contests and games along the course\, plus a silent auction before and aft
 er the tournament.</p><p>A<strong fr-original-style="" style="font-weight:
  700\;">&nbsp\;four-person team entry is $600</strong> includes breakfast
 \, lunch\, and 2 drinks per player. Lunch will be served following the tou
 rnament.&nbsp\;</p><p><strong fr-original-style="" style="font-weight: 700
 \;">Sponsorship Opportunities:</strong> We are currently looking for like-
 minded businesses to partner with us in sponsorship for the Golf FORE! Edu
 cation Golf Tournament. Sponsorship levels and participation range from a 
 $1\,500 award sponsor to a $150 tee sign. <em>Additionally\, we are accept
 ing donations of items for a silent auction.</em></p><p><strong fr-origina
 l-style="" style="font-weight: 700\;">About the Foundation:</strong> The <
 a fr-original-style="" href="https://www.sbchamberfoundation.org/" style="
 user-select: auto\;"><strong fr-original-style="" style="font-weight: 700
 \;">South Baldwin Chamber Foundation</strong></a> supports 11 public schoo
 ls in the Foley and Elberta feeder patterns\, along with three private sch
 ools in South Baldwin County. Our mission is to enhance lives through prog
 rams and partnerships that enrich education\, develop leadership\, and bet
 ter our community.</p><p><br /></p></body></html>\n\n---\n🌐 View origin
